{
  "abstract": "In 1979, Paul Erdős conjectured that powers of 2 avoid the ternary digit 2 only for n ∈ {0, 2, 8}. In the dual negative-power direction, we formalize the complete classification of ternary digit distributions for reciprocals 1/2^n: for all n ≥ 4, the base-3 expansion of 1/2^n contains the digit 2. The proof establishes the Gap Lemma for the coset {1, 3} mod 8 (maximum gap bounded by 6) and uses the Lifting-the-Exponent Lemma (LTE) to prove that the cyclic subgroup ⟨3⟩ mod 2^n surjects onto the entire coset {1, 3} mod 8, forcing the cyclic orbit to intersect the digit-2 target interval.",
  "authors": [
